1
00:00:00,880 --> 00:00:02,680
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:04,617
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:07,237
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer,

4
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:10,496
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,995
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,440
You can have it.

7
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:16,660
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,080
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,257
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

10
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:26,757
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,537
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:35,000
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

13
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:40,380
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for!

14
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:42,700
One piece.

15
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:52,717
Compass left behind,
it'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:58,437
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

17
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:01,117
That legendary place?

18
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,817
That the end of the map reveals.

19
00:01:03,900 --> 00:01:06,697
Is only legendary?

20
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:10,137
Till someone proves it real.

21
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:12,577
Through it all!

22
00:01:12,660 --> 00:01:14,517
Through all the trouble and times!

23
00:01:14,600 --> 00:01:16,837
Through the heartache
and through the pain!

24
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:21,337
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

25
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:24,280
Like I know you'll stand by me.

26
00:01:25,280 --> 00:01:30,620
So come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

27
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:36,060
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for!

28
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:42,460
There's always room for you
if you want to be my friend.

29
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:46,740
We are, we are on the crew.

30
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,720
We are

31
00:01:56,100 --> 00:01:58,760
This looks suspiciously
like a treasure map,

32
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:01,940
and it seems to be pointing
to Cocoyashi Village.

33
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:10,497
I can't believe you have the nerve
to go through my personal belongings.

34
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,797
That's my map, and it has
nothing to do with you.

35
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:13,710
So angry.

36
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,762
Is there something on your mind?

37
00:02:19,280 --> 00:02:20,720
What is this?

38
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,900
Why are all these guys
dead? What happened?

39
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:27,740
The pirate hunter Zoro did it.

40
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,000
Why weren't you here, Hachi? Huh?

41
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:34,137
This could have been
prevented had you been here.

42
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:37,500
Of course it could have,
had I only been here.

43
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:40,000
It's unforgivable.

44
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:41,370
We get it.

45
00:02:41,453 --> 00:02:43,377
You weren't here, so you
don't know where he is.

46
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:44,290
Is that right?

47
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:45,490
Whoa.

48
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:48,060
Well, let me think about it.

49
00:02:48,200 --> 00:02:49,460
I saw one guy.

50
00:02:49,660 --> 00:02:50,657
Yeah, that's right.

51
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:53,820
He was a slightly
suspicious swordsman type.

52
00:02:55,760 --> 00:02:57,060
Oh, that's him!

53
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,520
You did see him, you idiot!

54
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,918
So where did he go?

55
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:07,980
He told me he wanted to see Orlong, so
I gave him a ride to Cocoyashi Village.

56
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:11,930
Excellent.

57
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:14,549
That means we don't
have any need to hurry.

58
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:17,140
He's going to come straight to me.

59
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:22,077
Sorry, Orlong, but if I had known
you were going to be back so soon,

60
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,437
I would have kept him here for you.

61
00:03:23,520 --> 00:03:25,377
But he said he was a guest and I thought I

62
00:03:25,460 --> 00:03:28,284
should get him to the
village as fast as I could

63
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:29,470
Zoro, huh?

64
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:33,261
Which means if I could buy
just a little more time

65
00:03:38,380 --> 00:03:40,439
Why do you keep getting in the way?

66
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,958
Everything's so close to working out

67
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:45,520
So close!

68
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:57,670
Ugggh! Egh!

69
00:03:57,820 --> 00:03:58,860
Damn you, Nami!

70
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:00,397
You wanna fight, don't ya?

71
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:02,080
This is your fault, Dusak.

72
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:04,440
You're the one getting in the way.

73
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:07,207
This is what you get
for messing with Arlong!

74
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,320
Nami, you really disappointed me.

75
00:04:10,920 --> 00:04:15,097
Even after you stole our ship and ran
off, Luffy had complete faith in you!

76
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:18,697
He trusts you completely, and you
haven't even shown an ounce of guilt!

77
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:21,000
How can you betray someone like that?

78
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:22,557
Are you really that cold-hearted?

79
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:24,680
The only thing I trust is money.

80
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:27,377
Those dumb enough to be fooled deserve it.

81
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:28,800
How can you say that?

82
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:31,920
You idiots.

83
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,104
It was going according to plan.

84
00:04:36,440 --> 00:04:41,320
I'm not about to let you and your friends
ruin eight long years of hard work.

85
00:04:41,780 --> 00:04:43,200
So long, Usopp.

86
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,737
It's just business.

87
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:45,860
You understand.

88
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,500
Well, I'll be damned.

89
00:04:49,880 --> 00:04:52,557
Looks like you became a
pirate while you were gone.

90
00:04:52,640 --> 00:04:53,560
So long.

91
00:04:55,260 --> 00:04:57,380
What like you're gonna kill me?

92
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:01,057
That's right.

93
00:05:01,140 --> 00:05:03,257
I wouldn't underestimate me.

94
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:10,080
Oh Crap if I stay here, I'm
a dead man special attack

95
00:05:22,640 --> 00:05:23,581
Now's my chance.

96
00:05:26,900 --> 00:05:30,000
This is just like something
you'd think of. Nami!

97
00:05:32,700 --> 00:05:33,880
Don't do this.

98
00:05:40,720 --> 00:05:42,500
It's for my business.

99
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,617
This was my only choice.

100
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,880
Nami, how could you?

101
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:57,120
Now go and die.

102
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,960
I can't believe it.

103
00:06:11,300 --> 00:06:16,180
Big Tessnami killed Big Bro-O-Sup!

104
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:20,680
Your wish came true.

105
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,380
You died at sea.

106
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:25,480
Nami, I'm sorry for doubting you.

107
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:27,958
Without question, you're our friend.

108
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,330
Friend, huh?

109
00:06:29,700 --> 00:06:32,288
There's only one reason
I joined this group.

110
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:36,880
And that's to buy
Cocoyashi Village from you.

111
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:38,440
You got that?

112
00:06:38,580 --> 00:06:40,220
Just business, not friends.

113
00:06:41,660 --> 00:06:45,189
Keep your end of the deal, and
I'll have those berries soon.

114
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:46,760
Yes, of course.

115
00:06:47,060 --> 00:06:51,531
I'd rather cut my stomach open and die
than rake a promise concerning money.

116
00:06:51,700 --> 00:06:53,720
That's the kind of man I am.

117
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:55,940
Glad to hear it, Arlong.

118
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:57,318
You know the score.

119
00:07:00,220 --> 00:07:02,040
She gives me the creeps.

120
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:06,200
Oh, what a great woman she's become.

121
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:09,980
He's dead.

122
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:11,800
She killed him.

123
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,520
That witch killed him.

124
00:07:16,140 --> 00:07:18,080
Oh, there it is!

125
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:19,400
Arlo Park!

126
00:07:23,340 --> 00:07:24,170
Hey!

127
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:25,960
Keep up the pace, cow!

128
00:07:26,220 --> 00:07:27,700
I feel sorry for it.

129
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:30,477
Sanji's kicks must have
really taken their toll.

130
00:07:30,560 --> 00:07:31,480
Not that way!

131
00:07:31,700 --> 00:07:32,937
Go to your other left!

132
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:34,500
To the building, stupid!

133
00:07:57,260 --> 00:07:59,620
Oh, it's almost like we're flying!

134
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:00,970
Almost!

135
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:03,500
We are flying, you moron! No!

136
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:05,060
We're falling!

137
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,440
Man, they're successful!

138
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,240
Hey, girls!

139
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,180
Awesome! We're here, guys!

140
00:08:37,560 --> 00:08:42,860
What the hell were you doing?

141
00:08:43,660 --> 00:08:44,660
What do you mean?

142
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:47,060
We're here to pick up Nami. Duh.

143
00:08:47,300 --> 00:08:49,359
How come you haven't found her yet?

144
00:08:49,740 --> 00:08:50,570
Oh, yeah.

145
00:08:50,653 --> 00:08:52,287
What about Usopp and Johnny?

146
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:56,840
Usopp? Oh, no. Come
on. We've got to hurry.

147
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:58,710
Why?

148
00:08:58,793 --> 00:08:59,623
What's wrong?

149
00:08:59,706 --> 00:09:01,177
That dumbass has been caught by Arlong.

150
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:03,037
We've got to hurry before they kill him.

151
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:04,560
He's already dead.

152
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:07,130
What?

153
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:08,043
We're too late.

154
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:10,720
Big bro Usopp is dead.

155
00:09:15,220 --> 00:09:16,820
Tommy murdered him!

156
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:23,260
Come on, hurry up! What's the deal?

157
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:25,417
The marines are here, we're saved!

158
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:27,797
Some survivors from
Koza managed to contact

159
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:30,017
the government and they
told them what happened!

160
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:32,571
Now the marines are here to rescue us all!

161
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:34,430
See?

162
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,780
Finally, it's over!

163
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:41,433
Now we get to leave this horrible place!

164
00:09:45,560 --> 00:09:48,317
So this is the infamous arlong park.

165
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:53,077
What is the world coming to when pirate
skunk can set up such an opulent base?

166
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:54,917
Listen up, men.

167
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,417
Our noble mission today
is one of extraction.

168
00:09:57,500 --> 00:10:00,337
We must rescue the survivors
of the town of gosa,

169
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:03,157
which was savagely destroyed
by the arlong pirates.

170
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:09,297
But I am left to wonder would our
brand of swift and terrible justice

171
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:13,917
allow us to simply overlook the decadent
fortress of these unchecked brutes?

172
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,577
Sir? No. Sir. Correct.

173
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:20,157
Our unit must annihilate
arlong and his men.

174
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:22,357
Prepare for battle at once!

175
00:10:22,440 --> 00:10:23,517
Yes, sir.

176
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,757
Is that right?

177
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:26,117
Marine branch 77?

178
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,177
That's right.

179
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:28,317
That's what I said.

180
00:10:28,400 --> 00:10:29,357
A newcomer.

181
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:32,397
We'll have someone negotiate
with the man in charge.

182
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:36,017
If two million isn't enough to keep
them from trying anything funny,

183
00:10:36,100 --> 00:10:38,041
then kill every last one of them.

184
00:10:41,340 --> 00:10:42,240
Oh, no!

185
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:44,017
The marines have opened fire!

186
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:45,700
Orlog, watch out!

187
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:57,820
Whoa, he crushed a cannonball.

188
00:10:58,180 --> 00:10:59,880
Those jaws are terrifying.

189
00:11:00,620 --> 00:11:01,700
So what now?

190
00:11:01,940 --> 00:11:03,060
Are the talks...

191
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:06,150
...canceled?

192
00:11:06,233 --> 00:11:07,980
All right, let's do it!

193
00:11:09,220 --> 00:11:11,060
It's gonna be a bloodbath!

194
00:11:12,540 --> 00:11:13,577
Hold on, guys.

195
00:11:13,660 --> 00:11:14,800
Not so fast.

196
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:21,160
There's no need to expend so much
energy just to take out the trash.

197
00:11:22,060 --> 00:11:23,660
Just leave it to us.

198
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:26,857
What foolish humans they
are to pick a fight with us.

199
00:11:26,940 --> 00:11:28,320
In our own waters, too.

200
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:32,625
Those marines don't stand a chance
against three of our leaders.

201
00:11:32,840 --> 00:11:35,899
I doubt that ship will make
it a full three minutes.

202
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:39,317
That's odd.

203
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:41,677
Seems that cannonball was a dud.

204
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:42,590
Fire another!

205
00:11:42,673 --> 00:11:44,757
This is a signal of open hostility!

206
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,217
Never drop your guard!

207
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:47,537
When you're dealing with fishmen.

208
00:11:47,620 --> 00:11:48,450
Sir.

209
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:52,930
Mandel.

210
00:11:53,013 --> 00:11:53,843
It's one of them.

211
00:11:53,926 --> 00:11:56,460
Stand down! Right now!

212
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:59,617
One of our longsmen, yes.

213
00:11:59,700 --> 00:12:01,797
I am Commodore Perona Perona.

214
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:03,360
Of Marines Branch No.

215
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:09,220
77 Allow me to elaborate You see, we are
a somewhat well-known elite marine unit.

216
00:12:09,420 --> 00:12:11,977
Do you understand what
I'm telling you, fish man?

217
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:14,589
If you wish to live,
surrender immediately.

218
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:17,040
What have you done to him?

219
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,082
You killed him!

220
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:20,572
What's all this shaking?

221
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:23,564
Don't tell me there are
fish men under the ship.

222
00:12:26,580 --> 00:12:29,980
I really am sorry to
inconvenience you like this,

223
00:12:30,140 --> 00:12:32,957
but we just took the liberty
of removing your rudder.

224
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:33,870
Is that okay?

225
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,060
You what, Commodore?

226
00:12:37,740 --> 00:12:40,840
Don't worry, I didn't hit
any of his vital organs.

227
00:12:41,860 --> 00:12:43,566
Commodore, I have a question.

228
00:12:43,840 --> 00:12:45,757
It's just hypothetical, of course.

229
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:49,605
If one were to move a large reef
directly into a strong current,

230
00:12:49,720 --> 00:12:52,177
what do you suppose would
happen to the ocean?

231
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:53,090
What?

232
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:59,500
No, moving the whole reef?

233
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:00,798
That can't be done.

234
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:02,017
It's just not possible.

235
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:04,780
Put it down over there, Haji. Right.

236
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:09,560
Uh, Commodore, a giant
whirlpool's just appeared.

237
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,117
The rudder isn't working.

238
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,030
What?

239
00:13:12,113 --> 00:13:14,140
I told you, we removed the rudder.

240
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:20,720
So now this rudderless ship is
headed straight to the sea floor.

241
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:39,760
You're dead!

242
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:43,620
That's right, and so is hope.

243
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,240
Time to face the truth.

244
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:49,129
There's no way to escape
Barlong's control.

245
00:13:52,780 --> 00:13:54,140
I'll bet you're tired.

246
00:13:54,380 --> 00:13:56,262
No, I didn't even break a sweat.

247
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:59,377
We know everything about these
waters, from the winds to the depths.

248
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:00,337
It was quite easy.

249
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:04,220
With our expert knowledge of
these waters, no one can beat us.

250
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:06,940
True, but let's not forget Nami's charts.

251
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:09,380
Indeed, they are excellent charts.

252
00:14:09,700 --> 00:14:12,837
If we could persuade Nami to do
this for all the world's oceans,

253
00:14:12,920 --> 00:14:16,038
we would be the undisputed
rulers of the sea forever.

254
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,240
I know, Nami's brilliant.

255
00:14:19,480 --> 00:14:22,777
In fact, she could be critical in
the creation of the Arlong Empire.

256
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,800
It's just a shame. A shame?

257
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,277
He promised to let Nami
and Cocoyashi Village

258
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:30,184
go while she saves up a
hundred million berries.

259
00:14:30,420 --> 00:14:31,620
Oh, no, seriously?

260
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,017
Whatever you do, you can't let her leave!

261
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:34,930
You can't!

262
00:14:35,013 --> 00:14:35,843
I have to.

263
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:38,720
That's what we agreed
upon eight years ago.

264
00:14:39,340 --> 00:14:43,575
I'm the kind of man who always keeps
my promises when it comes to money.

265
00:14:44,540 --> 00:14:45,370
Always.

266
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:48,520
Say another word and you'll regret it!

267
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:49,640
Easy, Luffy.

268
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,717
This has nothing to do with Johnny.

269
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:53,800
Go on, believe whatever you want.

270
00:14:54,020 --> 00:14:55,580
But I know what I saw!

271
00:14:55,860 --> 00:14:58,697
Nami killed big bro Osop! Shut your mouth!

272
00:14:58,780 --> 00:15:01,800
Never in a million years
would Nami kill Usopp!

273
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,857
She wouldn't do that to her friends!

274
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,580
But I saw it!

275
00:15:07,060 --> 00:15:09,119
What was that about friends, Luffy?

276
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:10,510
Nami!

277
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:12,320
What are you doing here?

278
00:15:12,540 --> 00:15:13,817
What are we doing here?

279
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:15,080
You're our friend!

280
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:16,740
We came to get you.

281
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,100
What a pest. Nami?

282
00:15:19,880 --> 00:15:20,710
Friends, huh?

283
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,120
Don't make me laugh.

284
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:25,261
You're just pathetic enough
to deserve each other.

285
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:26,730
Damn you!

286
00:15:26,813 --> 00:15:28,260
You killed him!

287
00:15:28,380 --> 00:15:29,680
I watched you do it!

288
00:15:29,920 --> 00:15:32,960
And now, Big Bro Osup is gone!

289
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,259
Yep, that's right.

290
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:37,086
So why don't you kill
me and get your revenge?

291
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:38,490
What?

292
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:43,140
Word to the wise fellas, because
of your friend's stupidity,

293
00:15:43,620 --> 00:15:47,149
Arlong is preparing to kill
Zoro along with his entire crew.

294
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:51,186
And I don't care how monstrously
strong you guys think you are,

295
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:53,535
you're no match for the real monsters.

296
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,020
Hi, Nami!

297
00:15:58,380 --> 00:15:59,640
It's me, Sanji!

298
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,252
Let's run away together!

299
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:02,560
Can it, Romeo?

300
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:04,657
This isn't the time or place for that!

301
00:16:04,740 --> 00:16:05,720
Excuse me.

302
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:08,460
Love is like a hurricane, so back off!

303
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:10,417
Hey, look at me when I'm talking to you!

304
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:11,735
Nami, where is Usopp?

305
00:16:12,160 --> 00:16:13,880
With the fishes. Damn it!

306
00:16:13,980 --> 00:16:14,880
Cut the crap!

307
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:18,740
How sad.

308
00:16:19,140 --> 00:16:20,820
A swordsman striking a lady.

309
00:16:21,780 --> 00:16:22,610
Idiot!

310
00:16:22,693 --> 00:16:24,197
Can't you see what's happening here?

311
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:25,537
You're starting to piss me off!

312
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:29,900
If someone had stopped me
that easily, I'd be mad, too.

313
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,090
What?

314
00:16:32,173 --> 00:16:33,820
You should watch your mouth.

315
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:36,320
I'll say whatever I want, bastard.

316
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:38,100
Big bros!

317
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:39,917
We're all in this together, okay?

318
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,471
This is no time to fight!

319
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:42,560
Your pal's right.

320
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:45,157
Now quit your bickering and
leave while you still can.

321
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:48,897
You outsiders have no right to
butt into this island's affairs.

322
00:16:48,980 --> 00:16:50,217
Don't you get it yet?

323
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,977
The only reason I got
close to you idiots was

324
00:16:53,060 --> 00:16:55,537
so that I could rob you
of everything you had.

325
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:58,117
but now that you're broke, it
looks like the dream's dead.

326
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,660
So go, take your ship.

327
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:04,094
Go on, find a navigator dumb enough
to join you and go to the Grand Line.

328
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:07,753
Continue on your quest to find
the One Piece or whatever.

329
00:17:08,240 --> 00:17:10,540
Just leave here, you're an eyesore.

330
00:17:13,660 --> 00:17:14,700
Goodbye now.

331
00:17:16,240 --> 00:17:17,070
Nami.

332
00:17:23,940 --> 00:17:28,637
Big bro Luffy sleepy
sleep at a time like this

333
00:17:28,720 --> 00:17:31,544
in the middle of the road
well i'm pretty tired.

334
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:34,997
I'm not gonna butt into
their affairs i'm not

335
00:17:35,080 --> 00:17:39,320
interested but i'm not
leaving either night. Huh?

336
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:46,850
Fine.

337
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:48,510
Whatever!

338
00:17:48,660 --> 00:17:50,360
Just go ahead and die! No!

339
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,470
Hey!

340
00:17:56,553 --> 00:17:57,540
Big Bro Zoro!

341
00:17:57,780 --> 00:18:00,200
What on earth are you thinking? Come on!

342
00:18:00,420 --> 00:18:02,917
Did you forget that
Arlong is out to kill us?

343
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:04,337
We should be running away!

344
00:18:04,420 --> 00:18:06,797
Now that we know what Nami's really like,

345
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:10,821
there isn't a single good reason
why we should stay on this island.

346
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:14,550
Right.

347
00:18:14,633 --> 00:18:15,463
Understood.

348
00:18:15,546 --> 00:18:17,397
Sorry to cut our reunion
short, but I won't stay.

349
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,037
My role as guide ends here.

350
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,380
Yeah, I'm with him.

351
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:23,940
I don't want to deliberately
get myself killed. Fine.

352
00:18:24,360 --> 00:18:25,536
I'll see you around.

353
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:28,226
Until we meet again, big bro!

354
00:18:28,380 --> 00:18:30,500
Take care, you guys! You too.

355
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:51,000
Hey, do you still honestly believe
that Nami could have killed Usopp?

356
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:59,660
When she did that...

357
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,980
It's for my business.

358
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:06,920
This was my only choice.

359
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:10,800
When she did that,

360
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:15,467
Nami stabbed her own hand to
make it look like she stabbed me.

361
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:20,298
I can't believe she did that for me.

362
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:21,977
But it's a good thing she did.

363
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:24,757
Otherwise, I'd be fish
food right now for sure.

364
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:25,980
But what do I do?

365
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:30,181
A manly man like me can't just turn
tail and run after being saved.

366
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:31,480
One step at a time.

367
00:19:31,720 --> 00:19:34,073
Right now, I gotta hurry and find Zoro.

368
00:19:34,620 --> 00:19:37,780
Is that him up ahead? It is! It's Zoro!

369
00:19:38,820 --> 00:19:40,400
So Nami didn't kill him?

370
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,837
Is that what you're saying?

371
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:42,750
Am I wrong?

372
00:19:43,380 --> 00:19:44,580
Well, who knows?

373
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:46,737
I always thought of her as kind of a small

374
00:19:46,820 --> 00:19:49,017
-time crook who wouldn't
even watch a guy die,

375
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:50,097
let alone kill him.

376
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:51,768
But maybe she just snapped.

377
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:53,255
Wait, what'd you say?

378
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:55,140
She's not small-time!

379
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,480
Is she all you think of?

380
00:20:02,320 --> 00:20:03,277
He's alive!

381
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:04,840
Well, he was.

382
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,680
I hope he still is.

383
00:20:25,780 --> 00:20:27,040
Geez, Nami.

384
00:20:27,280 --> 00:20:29,339
You sure know how to trash a place.

385
00:20:29,900 --> 00:20:31,817
Hey, what's wrong?

386
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:32,820
Nothing.

387
00:20:33,180 --> 00:20:35,415
I'm just resting a little, that's all.

388
00:20:36,140 --> 00:20:38,397
You mean to tell me that
pouring over a treasure

389
00:20:38,480 --> 00:20:41,068
map after wrecking a
house is how you relax?

390
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:44,580
You're not fooling me.

391
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:46,036
Now Vice up already.

392
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:47,375
What's bothering you?

393
00:20:49,580 --> 00:20:50,480
It's okay.

394
00:20:50,760 --> 00:20:52,819
You can tell me anything, remember?

395
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:55,217
Something happened to make me mad.

396
00:20:55,300 --> 00:20:56,130
It's nothing.

397
00:20:57,860 --> 00:20:59,860
Those guys. Who are they?

398
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,080
You know?

399
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:03,940
Yeah, I met some captain guy.

400
00:21:04,520 --> 00:21:06,579
He seemed kind of liar-ish, though.

401
00:21:12,780 --> 00:21:14,200
Now I see.

402
00:21:15,620 --> 00:21:18,140
Yeah, that would hit her heart.

403
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:21,242
To think that someone
actually showed up for her.

404
00:21:23,040 --> 00:21:23,870
Friends.

405
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:30,060
That word means pain.

406
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:33,500
It breaks her heart.

407
00:21:35,620 --> 00:21:36,450
Usopp!

408
00:21:36,840 --> 00:21:38,580
Did Nami do all this to you?

409
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:41,700
Sorry, Zoro and I did that. No, you did.

410
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:44,880
Luffy, you're here now.

411
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,420
Yep, sure am.

412
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:48,500
I'm here too. Hi there.

413
00:21:48,620 --> 00:21:50,561
One of these days, I'll kill you.

414
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,860
Oh, you just made a
full recovery. Shut up!

415
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:58,037
Oh, and by the way, we kind of
heard you were dead, killed by Nami.

416
00:21:58,120 --> 00:22:01,477
Stupid Johnny, he was spouting
nonsense that entire time.

417
00:22:01,560 --> 00:22:04,900
Well, in a way, it is the truth.

418
00:22:06,040 --> 00:22:10,117
But I'm alive, cause you see,
she actually saved my life.

419
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:12,657
Looks to me like she's got
some sort of hidden motive

420
00:22:12,740 --> 00:22:15,377
for hanging out with a
bunch of renegade fishmen.

421
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:16,290
Obviously?

422
00:22:16,373 --> 00:22:17,340
Fine, what next?

423
00:22:17,540 --> 00:22:19,217
We're gonna destroy Arlong Park?

424
00:22:19,300 --> 00:22:20,657
Whoa, hang on just a second,

425
00:22:20,740 --> 00:22:23,397
don't you think we better find out
what's going on with Nami first?

426
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:25,500
It's no use either way Huh?

427
00:22:25,780 --> 00:22:30,320
No matter what you guys do, Arlong's
rule won't come to an end. No, Gecko.

428
00:22:30,860 --> 00:22:31,690
Who's she?

429
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:33,460
Nami's big sister. What?

430
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:34,520
Nami's sister?

431
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:36,100
No wonder she's so hot.

432
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,480
What do you mean that it's no use?

433
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:39,740
Just trust me.

434
00:22:39,900 --> 00:22:42,197
Don't get yourselves involved
in what's going on here.

435
00:22:42,280 --> 00:22:43,809
And leave poor Nami alone.

436
00:22:44,140 --> 00:22:45,840
I'll explain the situation.

437
00:22:46,100 --> 00:22:49,057
And if that doesn't get you to
leave, I don't know what will.

438
00:22:49,140 --> 00:22:49,970
Look!

439
00:22:50,053 --> 00:22:51,877
There's a marine ship at the shore!

440
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:53,397
It's Bridge 16th ship!

441
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:58,009
Maybe headquarters is finally taking
action after what happened to Branch 77.

442
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:04,660
I'm Colonel Nezumi of Branch 16.

443
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:09,580
Now then, Genzo, please step up
and make it snappy. Yes, Colonel.

444
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:11,824
I'm the one you're looking for.

445
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:13,290
You, huh?

446
00:23:13,373 --> 00:23:17,440
Take me to Nami's house
at once. Nami? But why?

447
00:23:17,620 --> 00:23:20,208
I don't understand
what's going on, Colonel.

448
00:23:21,100 --> 00:23:22,180
Lead the way.

449
00:23:22,420 --> 00:23:24,240
That is all you need to do.

450
00:23:50,880 --> 00:23:53,077
As I watched the sunrise,

451
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:56,897
I began to wonder What could be

452
00:23:56,980 --> 00:24:00,280
the reason it's so hot inside?

453
00:24:00,700 --> 00:24:06,337
No answer has come, but I can't
get away from what's true.

454
00:24:06,420 --> 00:24:08,840
It's because of you!

455
00:24:11,700 --> 00:24:16,437
Show me how to catch those feelings,
get them to come back to me?

456
00:24:16,520 --> 00:24:18,797
I'll do what I must be.

457
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:21,517
Cause they're everything I want will be!

458
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:24,057
Pack these arms around my dreams.

459
00:24:24,140 --> 00:24:26,117
And pull us back from yesterday.

460
00:24:26,200 --> 00:24:31,500
If I'm holding hands with you,
I'm sure that we can make the way.
